TITLE:: FluidModelComposer
summary:: Join several FluidModels into one searchable corpus
categories:: Libraries>FluidModel
related:: Classes/FluidModel

DESCRIPTION::
A FluidModelComposer merges the datasets, labels and slice positions of several built (or loaded) link::Classes/FluidModel::s into a new FluidModel, link::#-model::, so that slices from all of them can be plotted, searched and filtered together. Nothing is re-analysed and no audio is copied.

Slice identifiers keep the key of the model they come from (code::'drums-3'::, code::'voice-12'::), so the actions of the merged model's link::Classes/FluidModel#-plot:: and link::Classes/FluidModel#-reduceDimension:: receive the emphasis::original:: model of each slice, whose link::Classes/FluidModel#-buffer:: and link::Classes/FluidModel#-getSlice:: give the audio. For this to work the models must have Symbol keys and be registered (link::Classes/FluidModel#*new::), and their keys must differ.

note::
The merge runs asynchronously; give it a moment (or code::s.sync::) before using link::#-model::. The merged model only has datasets, link::Classes/FluidModel#-labelset:: and link::Classes/FluidModel#-slice_cache::: it has no buffers, so call playback methods on the original models (as the action arguments do).
::


CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Merge the models.

ARGUMENT:: models
An link::Classes/Array:: of link::Classes/FluidModel::s, all built or loaded.

returns:: A FluidModelComposer.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: model
The merged link::Classes/FluidModel::, registered under the String key code::"merged-<key1>_<key2>..."::.

METHOD:: models
The Array of source models.

METHOD:: plot
Plot the merged model: same as code::model.plot(dataset, algo, grid, neighbors, action):: (see link::Classes/FluidModel#-plot::), with a grid by default. Use code::model.plot:: directly for an code::upAction::.

ARGUMENT:: dataset
Dataset name, Array of names, link::Classes/FluidDataSet:: or code::nil:: (code::\merged::).

ARGUMENT:: algo
code::\pca::, code::\umap:: or code::\mds::.

ARGUMENT:: grid
Grid oversampling; 0 turns the grid off. Defaults to 1 here.

ARGUMENT:: action
As in link::Classes/FluidModel#-plot::: called with code::(model, slice)::, where code::model:: is the original model of the slice; without an action the nearest slice is posted.

ARGUMENT:: neighbors
Number of slices looked up per mouse position (with more than 1, code::action:: gets an Array of identifiers).

returns:: An link::Classes/Event:: with code::\plotter:: and code::\redux::.

METHOD:: reduceDimension
Same as code::model.reduceDimension(n, algo, dataset, grid, neighbors, action):: (see link::Classes/FluidModel#-reduceDimension::).

ARGUMENT:: n
Number of dimensions.

ARGUMENT:: algo
code::\pca::, code::\umap:: or code::\mds::.

ARGUMENT:: dataset
Dataset name, Array of names, link::Classes/FluidDataSet:: or code::nil::.

ARGUMENT:: grid
Grid oversampling; 0 turns the grid off.

ARGUMENT:: action
Called with the result Event.

ARGUMENT:: neighbors
Number of slices returned by code::find::.

returns:: An link::Classes/Event::, as link::Classes/FluidModel#-reduceDimension::.

METHOD:: init
Called by link::#*new::. Starts the merge.

METHOD:: prMergeModels
Private. Does the merge.

EXAMPLES::

code::
// build two models from different folders (or load stored ones)
(
s.waitForBoot {
	~drums = FluidModel(\drums);
	~voice = FluidModel(\voice);
	// one build at a time
	~drums.build("/path/to/drums", action: {
		"drums ready".postln;
		~voice.build("/path/to/voices", action: { "voices ready".postln });
	});
};
)

// when both are ready
~both = FluidModelComposer([~drums, ~voice]);

~both.model.datasets[\merged].print;
~both.model.labelset.print;

// play a slice from the model it belongs to
(
SynthDef(\fluidSlice2, { |out = 0, buf, start = 0, dur = 0.2, amp = 0.3|
	var env = EnvGen.kr(Env([0, 1, 1, 0], [0.005, dur - 0.01, 0.005]), doneAction: 2);
	Out.ar(out, PlayBuf.ar(2, buf, BufRateScale.kr(buf), startPos: start) * env * amp);
}).add;

~playFrom = { |model, slice|
	var info = model.getSlice(slice);
	Synth(\fluidSlice2, [buf: model.buffer, start: info[1], dur: info[0] / model.buffer.sampleRate]);
};
)

// one map for both corpora; the action gets the model each slice comes from
(
var last;
~both.model.plot([\mfcc, \spectralShape], \umap, action: { |model, slice|
	if (slice != last) { last = slice; ~playFrom.(model, slice) };
});
)

// navigate it from code
~redux = ~both.reduceDimension(2, \pca, \mfcc, action: { "map ready".postln });
~redux.find([0.2, 0.8], { |model, slice| [model.key, slice].postln; ~playFrom.(model, slice) });

// filters and sorts work across both corpora
~quiet = ~both.model.filter(["loudness < -35"], action: { ~quiet.print });

// the composer's own plot (grid on by default); without an action the nearest slice is posted
~both.plot(\chroma);
::
